id: E2167
error_signature: handwritten configure exits with "Unknown option --oldincludedir" (or other injected --*dir argument) during Conan AutotoolsToolchain configure step
match_keywords: handwritten configure,Unknown option,--oldincludedir,--datarootdir,--libdir,--bindir,update_configure_args,AutotoolsToolchain,injected arguments,argument whitelist,conan 2
category: build-system,autotools,conan
severity: high
root_cause: Upstream configure is a hand-written script (not autoconf-generated) that validates its argument whitelist and aborts on unrecognized options. Conan 2.x AutotoolsToolchain unconditionally injects standard GNU directory arguments (--prefix --bindir --sbindir --libdir --includedir --oldincludedir --datarootdir); any argument outside the handwritten whitelist (most commonly --oldincludedir) makes configure exit with Unknown option before compilation starts.
rec_approach: In recipe generate(), drop the offending argument with the official Conan API tc.update_configure_args with value None before tc.generate(). Do not patch the configure script for this and do not hand-write an argument filter. Platform detection failures in the same handwritten configure are a separate concern handled by an E160-class platform patch.
solution_cmds: |
  # conanfile.py — drop arguments a handwritten configure rejects
  def generate(self):
      tc = AutotoolsToolchain(self)
      tc.update_configure_args({"--oldincludedir": None})
      tc.generate()
  # verify which args are injected: inspect the generated conf / configure help whitelist
verification: conan create runs the configure step without Unknown option and proceeds to compile; the recipe diff stays free of configure-related patches for this problem.
fallback: If several non-whitelisted arguments remain, map each with update_configure_args to None; patching the configure whitelist is a last resort and should be kept separate from platform-mapping patches.
doc_refs: E160,E232,E095
applies_to: ck,lzip-family,sqlite,any-handwritten-configure-upstream
last_updated: 2026-09-12
